    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Substantive due process is a critical legal concept that allows the Supreme Court to strike down laws, even if they follow proper procedure, if the underlying law infringes upon fundamental individual rights. It essentially protects certain core liberties, like the right to privacy or personal autonomy, from government overreach. By being a check on legislative power, this doctrine has been a powerful tool in the expansion of civil rights throughout American history. This helps ensure that the government cannot take away basic liberties without a very strong constitutional justification.",
      "source": "target",
